  "summary": "The Bay City Commission voted 6-2 on Nov. 17, 2025 to reject a two-year, $84,150 contract with Flock Safety for 13 license plate-reading cameras after strong public opposition. Residents and the ACLU raised privacy and data-sharing concerns, while the public safety director and Flock representatives defended the technology.",
